## Description

I sat down with Ultralytics’ Founder & CEO Glenn Jocher at YOLO Vision 2025 to unpack the new Ultralytics YOLO26 models and what they change for builders. While YOLO26 has been announced at YV25, the new models will become publicly available at the end of October 2025, so stay tuned!

During our interview with Glenn, we break down how the YOLO26 models differ from prior generations, what changed under the hood, and why it matters for training time, memory use, and results in production. Glenn explains the standout innovation in this line and how it helps with tougher cases like small objects, crowded scenes, and varied lighting.

We talk through where the impact lands first. Manufacturing quality checks, retail analytics, smart cities, drones, healthcare imaging, and safety use cases all see clear benefits. You will hear simple guidance on picking the right model size, setting up data, and moving from a pilot to a stable release.

We also cover what this launch means for the Ultralytics community. Glenn shares how the team is working with developers and researchers on feedback, documentation, and examples. 

Ultralytics recently closed a funding round, and we discuss the priorities that the investment supports, including product hardening, ecosystem tools, and education. Partnerships come up as a growth lever, with a focus on making deployment simpler across edge and cloud. 

We close on the 3 to 5-year view for the YOLO ecosystem and how the community will shape it. 

Learn more: https://docs.ultralytics.com/models/yolo26/

